---
description: Cut chat tokens without dropping facts, paths, or citations the work needs
alwaysApply: true
---

# Token efficiency

This rule is always on. Keep replies short. Keep required context. Do not spend tokens restating process.

## Keep (required context)

- Paths, symbols, skill IDs, offsets, error strings — exact
- Code citations for the lines you change or that prove the answer
- One-sentence outcome: what changed or what the answer is
- Ambiguity that would make a wrong edit: ask one targeted question

## Cut (noise)

- Recap of the user request, tool narration, “I will now”, option lists, hedging
- Repeating instructions already in other rules/skills
- Whole-file dumps, long logs, unused search hits
- Extra files “for context” after the edit site is known

## Explore

User pointers first (`@` files, open tabs, named paths). Then one tight Grep if needed. Read only the slice you will use (`offset`/`limit`). No explore-agent tours. No synonym/repo-wide searches. Stop searching when you can act.

## Reply shape

Lead with the answer or the change. Then only the citations/facts that support it. Simple questions: 1–2 sentences. Code, comments, commits, and docs stay normal prose — compress chat, not artifacts.

For extra compression in a session, the user can say `caveman` / `/caveman`.
